Shared teaching-page interface

Each lesson has its own app.R, numerical model.R, controls, interpretation,
and lecture reference. This file supplies only the consistent visual shell,
reproducible random-number scope, preset handling, and paused-by-default
animation controls. No remote fonts, JavaScript libraries, or R packages
beyond shiny and bslib are required.

Run any page with shiny::runApp("SelectionEffects"), replacing the directory
as needed. Local apps source ../TeachingTools/teaching.R. During Pages export
deploy.R bundles this shared source into each app so it runs independently
in the browser, without references outside its exported directory.

The root apps.R catalogue defines gallery ordering, lecture references, and
which apps need this shared source bundled. deploy.R exports all 20 pages
and generates docs/index.html from that catalogue. AstroInformatics.qmd
provides a matching source-page overview.

Tests:
  Rscript TeachingTools/test_numerics.R
  Rscript TeachingTools/test_pages.R
  Rscript TeachingTools/test_export.R (after Rscript deploy.R)

The numerical suite checks probability normalisation, exact updates, limiting
cases, simulation invariants, sampling distributions, and preservation of data
when inference or display settings change. The reactive suite exercises every
page, primary control boundaries, guided examples, plots, and animation.
